								<Wire Id="2305" Joints="N(2303:instance out)|(1044,185) h(16) v(70) N(394:110)|(1071,255)" xmlns="http://www.ni.com/PlatformFramework" />
								<Wire Id="2308" Joints="N(377:110)|(4,255) h(5) v(-70) N(552:instance in)|(379,185)" xmlns="http://www.ni.com/PlatformFramework" />
								<Comment Bounds="4 580 675 15" Id="2390" SizeToText="False" xmlns="http://www.ni.com/MocCommon">
									<p.Text>Register callback VIs to handle events from the Application Manager. Also register the Quit Application User Event.</p.Text>
								</Comment>
								<Comment Bounds="4 310 380 240" Id="2397" SizeToText="False" xmlns="http://www.ni.com/MocCommon">
									<p.Text>"To add new callbacks to handle additional TestStand events:\r\n1. Expand the Register Event Callback node.  \r\n2. Wire a reference to a manager control which defines the desired event (usually the ApplicationManager) to the Event terminal\r\n3. Click the event terminal to select the event to handle.\r\n4. Wire the UI Data cluster to the User Parameter terminal.  This allows the callback VI to access the data.\r\n5. Right Click the "VI Ref" Terminal and select Create Callback VI.  The generated GVI will execute when the event occurs.\r\n6. Modify the callback VI to implement the desired functionality\r\n\r\nRefer to the TestStand Help Topic "Customizing the LabVIEW NXG Simple User Interface" for more information on creating event callbacks."</p.Text>
								</Comment>
